{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WetDepLSColumn",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's large-scale wet deposition (wetdep_ls, wetscav_onoff = -1) over one column of the EqAtmChem configuration (chem_opt = 170), assembled from WetDepLS instances that share the column's cloud water, density, vertical velocity, geometry and grid-scale rain.\n\nwetdep_ls loops over species with nothing coupling one species to another: every instance forms the same column cloud-water flux and conversion factor from the same met, and the species differ only in their own burden gate and their efficiency (Par.alpha_sulf = 1 for gas-phase sulfuric acid, Par.alpha_aerosol = 0.5 for every aerosol species, nv > numgas). So this document is a MAPPING, and WetDepColumn's job is only to hold the column state once and hand it to each instance by variable_map; each instance's dc_dt = (c_out - c)/dt is the operator-split tendency a chemistry column adds to that species.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING, AND WHY. The scheme applies to 169 species of chem_opt 170 (sulf and the 168 MOSAIC aerosol species: eight sections of mass, number and water), and the esm format has no way to mount a component once per element of an index set: §10.5 lifting lifts a 0-D system over a grid, but WetDepLS is a column component whose burden and cloud-water integral are reductions over lev, and a species axis is neither the grid nor a 0-D lift. The alternatives are 169 hand-written mounts (a generated document, which this repo forbids) or giving WetDepLS a species axis (c over [lev, spc], alpha over [spc]), which is a change to the component and to its tests. This document therefore mounts SIX representative species -- sulf, so4_a03, nh4_a04, water_a05, oc_a07, num_a06 -- which exercise both efficiencies, a mass, a number and the water, and the full-species chemistry column waits on that decision.\n\nWhat the tests pin. Six steps of the separate wet-scavenging capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_wetscav.sh, the reference column with wetscav_onoff = -1 and cu_physics = 0, since the reference run has no wet scavenging and New Tiedtke makes all of its rain): the dry step 1300 and the event 1405-1480. Each instance's activation flag, scavenged column and tendency at 1e-9 of the column maximum against the real64 replay through chem/module_wetdep_ls.F; the fill script (tools/fill_wetdep_ls_column_tests.py) also checks that every species that changes anywhere in the dump is sulf or an aerosol species, which is the claim the mapping rests on (88 of 233 change during the event; the rest of the eligible 169 sit under the burden gate). Mutation checks: sulf at the aerosol efficiency fails 10 assertions, a number at the sulfuric-acid efficiency fails 10, one instance cut off from the vertical velocity fails 15, doubling the rain fails 36.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "wet deposition",
      "chem_opt 170",
      "coupling"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte; bound into every WetDepLS mount."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Par": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls_parameters.esm"
    },
    "Sulf": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV"
      }
    },
    "So4A03": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV"
      }
    },
    "Nh4A04": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV"
      }
    },
    "WaterA05": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV"
      }
    },
    "OcA07": {
